
<p>In the wake of <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/08/25/xcancel-cease-and-desist">Nitter/XCancel’s demise</a>, here’s a delightful new Safari extension from Zhenyi Tan (of And a Dinosaur fame):</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>But sometimes people still post X content. Maybe you want to see
<a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/08/12/google-design-pants-pissed">Gruber roast Google Design</a>. Maybe you want to see posts by
<a href="https://ticci.craft.me/explanation">Federico Viticci</a> who recently returned to X. So I made
Litterbox, a Safari extension that opens x.com links in a
popup. The idea is you open it, take a look, gag a little, then
close the lid. [...]</p>

<p>Litterbox doesn’t send your cookies when you open those popups,
because of course. It uses the same API X uses for its website
embeds. I don’t think they’ll kill the website embed feature. But
if they do, it will be very funny.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>I love it. I’ve got it installed even though I don’t avoid visiting X.com. It’s just faster and nicer to view tweets in Litterbox’s popup. And if I <em>do</em> want to proceed to X.com, there’s a link at the bottom of the popup. Perfect.</p>

